# Fear & Hunger - gamepad to keyboard, for gptokeyb2.
#
# The game is keyboard only: no gamepad plugin is enabled, and YEP_KeyboardConfig
# keeps RPG Maker MV's stock bindings. Z confirms, X cancels and opens the menu,
# Shift dashes, Q and W page through long lists, and DK_Name_Input adds backspace
# for the name entry screen.
#
# Face buttons follow the device's own labels, and so does the firmware: the
# RG40XX V's controller entry reads a:b1 b:b0, which maps SDL's A to the button
# printed A and SDL's B to the one printed B, rather than SDL's usual "A is the
# bottom button". So confirm goes on gptokeyb's b, which is the bottom button,
# the one a player's thumb rests on and the one printed B. Getting this the
# standard way round sends the menu key to the confirm button and makes battles
# unplayable: every press reads as cancel.

back = esc
start = esc

a = esc
b = enter
x = backspace
y = shift

l1 = q
r1 = w
l2 = pageup
r2 = pagedown

up = up
down = down
left = left
right = right

left_analog_up = up
left_analog_down = down
left_analog_left = left
left_analog_right = right

# Quitting is gptokeyb2's own START+SELECT combo, nothing to configure here.
